{"findings":[{"finding":"The PDF has to show 'no tax lines' because the spec picked ASM-50, but the accepted ASM-23 says the invoice shows VAT at a configurable rate; the spec settles this payments conflict with its own 'later wins' rule instead of asking the human.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Working days exclude 'configured public holidays' (ASM-49), which directly contradicts the accepted ASM-19 ('no holiday list in phase 1'); the spec resolves this itself rather than asking.","reqId":"REQ-29","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing says what happens when the ERP file is missing from the configured location, can't be read, or is the same file already imported the night before; only empty files and missing headers are covered (REQ-13).","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"For duplicate product codes it is unclear whether every duplicate row is rejected or only the second one, and no AC covers duplicates, so the stock value that ends up applied is undefined.","reqId":"REQ-13","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No behaviour is given for a report requested without a date range or with start after end (ASM-7 was never actually answered), and there is no error status for these cases.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing covers a customer with no assigned price list, or a product that isn't on the customer's price list, when viewing or ordering.","reqId":"REQ-30","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"'Authorised user' is never defined, and no AC checks that a user from another customer, or an unauthenticated caller, is denied GET /invoices/{id}/pdf, even though the risk tags include PII.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"There is no validation path for a missing, future-dated, or earlier-than-invoice-date payment date on mark-paid.","reqId":"REQ-27","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Sign-in failure is only handled through a generic message; there is no rate limiting or lockout for repeated failed attempts, despite the auth risk tag.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Only expiry is covered; nothing says what happens when a reset or invitation token is reused after it has already been consumed, or is tampered with.","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Rolling back the business action when the audit write fails is undefined for the 'ERP import failed' audit in REQ-15: there is no successful action to roll back, and the import status record could be lost.","reqId":"REQ-40","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-25.2 only says 'the response is an error' and doesn't give an observable status code or body.","reqId":"REQ-25","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The requirement refers to 'the listed customer, staff and admin screens', but the spec never lists them, so the AC can't be checked against a defined set.","reqId":"REQ-36","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The requirement says status is shown on the System/Import status screen, but AC-15.1 only checks the GET /admin/imports API and labels the test as job level, so the screen itself is never verified.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The 10 MB upload limit and the allowed file types are hard-coded in the requirement, while similar limits (link lifetimes, cut-off, payment term) are configuration.","reqId":"REQ-35","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The daily overdue job's run time and timezone are not specified, so the boundary for 'has passed' (for example, exactly 30 days) is ambiguous.","reqId":"REQ-26","rubric":2,"severity":"low"}],"note":"No OpenAI key: critic ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"}